From: Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>
Subject: [PATCH] net: lwip: seed the PRNG from the MAC address

The lwIP port maps LWIP_RAND() to rand() but never calls srand(), so every
board produces an identical sequence of "random" numbers. In particular, a
crate of identical boards powering up in lockstep presents the same DHCP
transaction ID (XID) to the server, from every board, in every discovery round.
Packet captures show a switch-hosted DHCP server failing to complete
REQUEST->ACK for most of a 16-board crate under these conditions, while a lone
board with a distinct XID obtained its lease immediately.

Call srand_mac() in net_init() before lwip_init(). The MAC-derived seed
guarantees distinct PRNG sequences across boards even with identical firmware
and fully synchronous boots.  Seeding before lwip_init() also decorrelates the
initial TCP/UDP ephemeral port bases, which are drawn during stack init, and
the DNS query IDs drawn later.

Signed-off-by: Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>
---
 net/lwip/net-lwip.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/lwip/net-lwip.c b/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
index 5fb06fc919d..bf00ecb9787 100644
--- a/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
+++ b/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
@@ -19,9 +19,12 @@
 #include <lwip/prot/etharp.h>
 #include <lwip/timeouts.h>
 #include <net.h>
+#include <rand.h>
 #include <timer.h>
 #include <u-boot/schedule.h>

+#include "../net_rand.h"
+
 /* xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx\0 */
 #define MAC_ADDR_STRLEN 18

@@ -293,6 +296,7 @@ int net_init(void)

 	if (!init_done) {
 		eth_init_rings();
+		srand_mac();
 		lwip_init();
 		init_done = true;
 	}
